{"id": "unknown-2026-07-31-015", "date": "2026-07-31", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 31, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["health_wellness", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "E. coli outbreak linked to frozen organic berries sold at Publix", "content": "<p>The FDA is investigating an outbreak of infections from E. coli O145:H28 that is related to imported, frozen berries sold at Publix stores.</p><p>The implicated berries are sold under the Greenwise brand and were imported from Frutas y Hortalizas del Sur S.A., of San Carlos, Chile, according to</p>", "sources": [{"name": "food_safety_news", "url": "https://www.foodsafetynews.com/2026/07/e-coli-outbreak-linked-to-frozen-organic-berries-sold-at-publix/", "type": "rss"}]}
