{"id": "unknown-2026-07-31-018", "date": "2026-07-31", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 31, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["food_safety", "health_wellness", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Imported organic berries recalled because of E. coli contamination and outbreak", "content": "<p>In relation to an outbreak of E. Coli infections, the Publix grocery store chain is recalling organic GreenWise imported frozen berries.</p><p>The outbreak has sickened 12 people in Florida and Georgia. Four of the patients have required hospitalization.</p><p>The recall applies to all frozen Greenwise organic blueberries and berry mixes</p>", "sources": [{"name": "food_safety_news", "url": "https://www.foodsafetynews.com/2026/07/imported-organic-berries-recalled-because-of-e-coli-contamination-and-outbreak/", "type": "rss"}]}
